# Licensing of the examples

The rest of this repository is under the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0
(see [../LICENSE](../LICENSE)). **These two files are not**, and cannot be:

- `latex_ocr_qwen3_5_vision.ipynb`
- `train_latex_ocr.py`

Both are derived from Unsloth's Qwen3.5-0.8B vision fine-tuning notebook, which
Unsloth publishes under the **GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0**:

> This notebook and all Unsloth notebooks are licensed LGPL-3.0
> — <https://github.com/unslothai/notebooks?tab=LGPL-3.0-1-ov-file#readme>

They keep substantial parts of that original — the installation cell, the
conversation-formatting function, the trainer configuration, the inference and
memory-statistics cells, and much of the prose. That makes them derivative works,
and LGPL-3.0 does not permit adding restrictions such as a noncommercial clause
to a work derived from it.

**So these two files remain under LGPL-3.0**, and you may use them commercially
on LGPL-3.0's terms, whatever the licence on the rest of the repository says.

The changes made to them — the `nawat` calls that replace the repo ids, output
paths and hyperparameters, and the commentary explaining why — are contributed
under LGPL-3.0 as well, so the files stay usable as a whole.

Nothing here restricts Unsloth itself: it is a separate work, installed
separately, under its own licence.

